data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"lookupStatus\": \"found\",\n    \"comments\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDozMDM2NjY5NTkzMTczNDgzXzMwMzY2NzQ5Mjk4Mzk2MTY=\",\n        \"text\": \"Get rid of the recruiting company first thing. Coaches hate dealing with them. You have to put in alot of work. Research colleges with his interested major, take virtual tours, etc. If interested in said school, send the coach an email and go from there. Like Robert said, be realistic about his ability and talent level. I know that's a hard one, but will help you narrow down the right fit for him. My son and I worked really hard to get him the right fit.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-06-14T22:29:41.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 2,\n        \"reactionCount\": 12,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Nicole Prieskorn\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid0FTj6GVEJMRJV16p7hFKFiJ2zfP2vTqMvWFwRQiLVpzqHPHQHtXqp3GCPRsqTohH9l\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Nicole\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDozMDM2NjY5NTkzMTczNDgzXzMwMzY3Nzg1Mjk4MjkyNTY=\",\n        \"text\": \"My heart goes out to you — this process is exhausting, especially when you’ve already invested so much. You’re not alone in this.\\n\\nCan I share something that might help? The AIQ — Athletic Intelligence Quotient — is a cognitive assessment built specifically for athletes. It gives your son a profile of how he’s wired: decision-making, processing speed, performance under pressure. More importantly, it gives him something concrete and compelling to bring to coaches that most kids simply don’t have.\\n\\nFor a rising senior still chasing an offer, that kind of edge matters. Happy to share more whenever you’re ready.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-06-15T01:19:38.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 3,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"DSH\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"61559474351822\",\n          \"shortName\": \"DSH\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDozMDM2NjY5NTkzMTczNDgzXzMwMzY3MDk5NjMxNjk0NDY=\",\n        \"text\": \"If you have spent money on a recruiting company then you have already made the investment and have a contract, so use them to finish this out. We used a recruiting agency and that is how my daughter got so many colleges interested in her because we had no idea how to do this process. We had flown to a tournament w college coaches and that opened the door but the agency is what allowed over 25 colleges/coaches to become interested in her. BUT, when we did this, she was in the middle of her senior year and we did not have a lot of time. I’m not sure what you mean by his hardheaded. There is still time but your son does have to be realistic about his abilities. Her Background…daughter was a multiple sports player but began private tennis lessons the summer of her freshman year. She was a natural but tennis is not a sport you just “pick up” and are fabulous at it. The hardest one she has played, she says. She quit her other sports, except goalie in soccer her Sophomore year. After that, she dropped everything else to focus because she was already behind. Traveled 1:40 hrs one way 2-3 days a week for lessons. After finishing her last senior year at State and recuperating from a bone bruise, she hit it hard and that’s when we started the recruiting process. She was not a D1 player. D2 would have been a stretch though several colleges were interested in her. NAIA was our goal. She visited 3 NAIA schools in the surrounding states and two D3. D3 was more $$$ and of course there is no scholarship money. Her gpa was really good and her ACT was good but not 32+ good. Merit scholarships would help but still more $. The school she is going to in the fall offered a ￼scholarship and she negotiated with them. It is an amazing program that seems to want to continue helping her develop, where some of the other schools offered her, just wanted her to play. I know this is a lot but I hope it helps!\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-06-14T23:26:49.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 2,\n        \"reactionCount\": 2,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Dawn Franks Harris\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"1378524435\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Dawn\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDozMDM2NjY5NTkzMTczNDgzXzMwMzY2ODM3MDY1MDU0MDU=\",\n        \"text\": \"No recruiting company needed! What do you mean by hard-headed? That may help us figure out how to help. Please be sure he actually wants to play in college and is willing to put in the time to send emails, fill our recruiting forms, get on calls with coaches, go on visits, etc.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-06-14T22:43:21.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 2,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Olga Norstrom\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid0c6zkX6kSEES16xjB699d1BgCNi7dHq29sqfCn2QnhsZGjWDongWruVdoUqFbJx7Al\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Olga\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDozMDM2NjY5NTkzMTczNDgzXzMwMzY4MTYzMjk4MjU0NzY=\",\n        \"text\": \"Which sport?\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-06-15T02:16:24.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 1,\n        \"reactionCount\": 0,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Rich-Lauri Pudleiner\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid02ZJASiwBQSGrcVuEhVBpi7zgRyHNbH7Gdp9cEjY1ysfYfPkbTtziCxZESQ8PEu6F2l\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Rich-Lauri\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDozMDM2NjY5NTkzMTczNDgzXzMwMzY2NzE4NTk4Mzk5MjM=\",\n        \"text\": \"By realistically assessing his level of play.  It’s likely you’re hunting too big a school.  Court D2 and D3, NAIA.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-06-14T22:25:00.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 5,\n        \"reactionCount\": 2,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Robert Stiers\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"pfbid0WmiMrNynvg8jvHXWGc4bmcxwCvJFcvUeV67GSxjS8jVBA7JgJRLAkUQUMVCCPE4bl\",\n          \"shortName\": \"Robert\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDozMDM2NjY5NTkzMTczNDgzXzMwMzc0MjEzOTk3NjQ5Njk=\",\n        \"text\": \"CAEA Sports Consulting Group I was a parenting just like you navigating the recruiting process for my son who is now a senior defensive tackle at University of Texas El Paso. I have helped 22 other clients also who have obtained football scholarships if you need assistance please feel free to reach out and we can discuss over a free consultation.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-06-15T15:53:02.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 0,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"CAEA Sports Consulting Group\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"61560801914251\",\n          \"shortName\": \"CAEA Sports Consulting Group\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDozMDM2NjY5NTkzMTczNDgzXzMwMzY3ODQyMDY0OTUzNTU=\",\n        \"text\": \"Start sending his hudl highlights to coaches’ IG. Copy and paste and send. Thats how my son got some of his offers.\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-06-15T01:28:12.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 0,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Anonymous participant 875\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"1593983055504549\",\n          \"shortName\": null\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDozMDM2NjY5NTkzMTczNDgzXzMwMzY3Mjg1MDk4MzQyNTg=\",\n        \"text\": \"Get rid of the recruiting company.. during our process it seems like coaches don’t want to talk to them, only the athlete. Mine is a committed d1 2027\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-06-14T23:59:06.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 0,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"AnonymousMom2027\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"36386398307642356\",\n          \"shortName\": null\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"Y29tbWVudDozMDM2NjY5NTkzMTczNDgzXzMwMzY2NzY4NDk4Mzk0MjQ=\",\n        \"text\": \"Thank you so much for the advice\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-06-14T22:32:39.000Z\",\n        \"replyCount\": 0,\n        \"reactionCount\": 0,\n        \"repliesCursor\": \"\",\n        \"author\": {\n          \"name\": \"Fiesty_Booksygirlie\",\n          \"platformUserId\": \"3021147984747150\",\n          \"shortName\": null\n        }\n      }\n    ],\n    \"page\": {\n      \"nextCursor\": \"MToxNzkzOTg0NjAxOgF_uT0irkrpdFQFgRtQW3ZG5jUDY-j6wyZid_JlPn6MEAmMOXsWK54ueuuwiLzdrmwEqIZ8OSpFlycSojOdyg3S6BpTmTY-PDmnq3eGROPrO-m13IK99zzD5KiaTWWUZJFBQ8nrizwKoQRlBtsqqyYKFmLh1yGlMdw83MDspUU0PzWSe67-PKHCbtIzhlz4GkvE6KmQGnB_Ev3SpVyXf11qQlm9ZpLOhQCt8pXkegIrIus8-uzdwXFMR2tXBLPlmFTRCe9ZHna3qmIth21XuVjUmPTPaG5OJF2M62ZTDdCL68XBw93w02iNz_Rc4sZFaqmUFWgcs9U56hbahw-YwEoq9lan2uLT7MaRk06iB43vqe1lp7NWbcHxLQDvhRutaS69fjjRThlGNTNg3BwcTctdOmosQYWSw0U1LIXi0nSHpZMq_cEOhFtEZM0\",\n      \"hasMore\": true\n    }\n  },\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"requestId\": \"req_0102a233-b4e4-4232-9cf7-b583bc49605d\",\n    \"creditsCharged\": 1,\n    \"version\": \"v1\"\n  }\n}"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"conversation_id\":\"01a1b1d0-952d-70c8-85c9-ca344565d1bb\"}"}],"structuredContent":{"data":{"lookupStatus":"found","comments":[{"id":"Y29tbWVudDozMDM2NjY5NTkzMTczNDgzXzMwMzY2NzQ5Mjk4Mzk2MTY=","text":"Get rid of the recruiting company first thing. Coaches hate dealing with them. You have to put in alot of work. Research colleges with his interested major, take virtual tours, etc. If interested in said school, send the coach an email and go from there. Like Robert said, be realistic about his ability and talent level.